target:    tests/bench/lib/pinned-columns.php
gate:      composer test:export-fidelity
kind:      restore-defect
expect:    NOT NULL is derived as not-nullable
rationale: Replaces the derived nullability with a constant `true`, so every pinned column reads as NULLable. REGISTERED BECAUSE THE GATE COULD NOT SEE IT: the TYPE half of the derivation was asserted and this half was not, so this exact change left the gate byte-identical at its assertion count while the real slim_stats manifest hash moved 5e984655 -> 7c88d02b. slimstat_fp2_kind() cannot catch it either - it truncates at the first space, so `VARCHAR(39) DEFAULT NULL` and `VARCHAR(39)` are the same string to it. Nullability is half of what the manifest hash claims about a schema, and it was travelling on nothing. Three shapes are pinned now: NOT NULL present, DEFAULT NULL present, and no NULL keyword at all - the last being the case the stripos rule gets right without the keyword appearing.
---
diff --git a/tests/bench/lib/pinned-columns.php b/tests/bench/lib/pinned-columns.php
--- a/tests/bench/lib/pinned-columns.php
+++ b/tests/bench/lib/pinned-columns.php
@@ -53,7 +53,7 @@
             // fingerprint would be guessing at, and a guessed type is a hash that means nothing.
             throw new RuntimeException("cannot read a declared type out of `{$name} {$fragment}`");
         }
-        return [$type, false === stripos($fragment, 'NOT NULL')];
+        return [$type, true];
     }
 
     /**
